      "title": "Part-Time Faculty, Exercise Science",
      "description": "Curry College\nJob Posting: Part-Time Faculty, Exercise Science Curry College \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Faculty, Exercise Science Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Faculty, Exercise Science Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Exercise Science Locations: Milton, MA Posted: Sep 21, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position ID: 205015 Share About Curry College: Curry College, founded in 1879, is a private, four-year, liberal arts-based institution in Milton, Massachusetts. Curry is the only college in Massachusetts to guarantee students a job after graduation via The Curry Commitment program. The College is accredited by the New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE) and offers 28 undergraduate majors, over 50 minors and concentrations, seven graduate programs, and an associate's degree. The College boasts a wide array of co-curricular activities including 40+ student-run clubs and organizations and 19 NCAA Division III athletic teams. The Curry College mission is to educate and graduate students prepared to engage in successful careers and active citizenship with a global perspective. We are an inclusive community of diverse learners and educators, committed to continuing our legacy of developing effective communicators with reflective and critical thinking skills. We mentor and empower our students, building meaningful relationships that inspire them to achieve their ambitions. Curry College provides rigorous and relevant academic programs to undergraduate and graduate students, and our rich blend of liberal arts and career-directed programs is enhanced by practical field experiences and co-curricular activities. Learning at Curry extends beyond the classroom and is embedded in all that we do. Diversity and a culture of equity and inclusion among students, faculty and staff are crucial to the mission statement of Curry College. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, sex identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law, including Title IX. Job Description: Curry College has ongoing needs for part-time Faculty to teach in our Exercise Science program. Our curriculum prepares students for careers in strength and conditioning, clinical exercise physiology, rehabilitation sciences, fitness and wellness, and graduate study in allied health professions (e.g., physical therapy, occupational therapy, physician assistant, athletic training, and related fields). All of our courses are taught in person on our Milton, MA campus. Days and hours of courses vary from semester to semester. Part-time Faculty are responsible for planning and presenting course material for assigned lecture, laboratory, and/or applied experiential courses; defining specific course requirements and communicating them clearly to students; evaluating student performance on examinations, projects, laboratory competencies, and practical assessments; submitting grades in a timely manner; and providing students with clear feedback regarding their progress. Part-time Faculty are expected to be available to interact electronically with students outside the classroom and to support student professional development. Courses available may include, but are not limited to: Kinesiology, Biomechanics, Exercise Physiology, Strength & Conditioning, Exercise Testing & Exercise Programming, Clinical Exercise Physiology, Nutrition for Health and Fitness, Performance Nutrition in Exercise and Sport, Research Methods in Exercise Science, Prevention and Care of Sports Injuries, etc. Requirements: Requirements: Minimum of a Master's degree* in a field related to Exercise Science. Examples include but are not limited to: Nutrition, Exercise Physiology, Physical Therapy, Strength and Conditioning, Human Performance, Biomechanics, Kinesiology, etc. Candidates should demonstrate relevant professional experience in fitness, performance, clinical, research or rehabilitation settings. If applicable, candidate should demonstrate and maintain current nationally recognized professional certification or licensure appropriate to their professional area Teaching experience is preferred, but not required. *In certain cases, candidates with a Bachelor's degree and substantial professional experience may be considered. Salary: $4,500 per 3 credit course *Please note: Eligibility for promotion to Lecturer and an increased rate of compensation are negotiated between the College and the Curry College AAUP. Additional Information: Committed to attracting and retaining a diverse staff, Curry College will honor your experiences, perspectives and unique identity. Together, our community strives to create and maintain working and learning environments that are inclusive, equitable and welcoming. At the College's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be excepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the College, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Employment in this position is contingent upon the successful completion of all required pre-employment background checks. Title IX Notice of Nondiscrimination Curry College (the \"College\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits sex discrimination in any education program or activity that we administer, as required by Title IX and its federal regulations, including in admission and employment. The Non-Discrimination Policy can be found at https://www.curry.edu/assets/Documents/About-Us/Curry-College-Nondiscrimination-Policy.pdf The Sexual Misconduct Policy can be found at https://www.curry.edu/assets/Documents/About-