      "title": "Associate Lecturer, Education (General Pool)",
      "description": "Curry College\nJob Posting: Associate Lecturer, Education (General Pool) Curry College \n\tJob Posting: Associate Lecturer, Education (General Pool) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Lecturer, Education (General Pool) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Education Locations: Milton, MA Posted: Sep 25, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 193267 Share About Curry College: Curry College, founded in 1879, is a private, four-year, liberal arts-based institution in Milton, Massachusetts. Curry is the only college in Massachusetts to guarantee students a job after graduation via The Curry Commitment program. The College is accredited by the New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE) and offers 28 undergraduate majors, over 50 minors and concentrations, seven graduate programs, and an associate's degree. The College boasts a wide array of co-curricular activities including 40+ student-run clubs and organizations and 19 NCAA Division III athletic teams. The Curry College mission is to educate and graduate students prepared to engage in successful careers and active citizenship with a global perspective. We are an inclusive community of diverse learners and educators, committed to continuing our legacy of developing effective communicators with reflective and critical thinking skills. We mentor and empower our students, building meaningful relationships that inspire them to achieve their ambitions. Curry College provides rigorous and relevant academic programs to undergraduate and graduate students, and our rich blend of liberal arts and career-directed programs is enhanced by practical field experiences and co-curricular activities. Learning at Curry extends beyond the classroom and is embedded in all that we do. Diversity and a culture of equity and inclusion among students, faculty and staff are crucial to the mission statement of Curry College. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, sex identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law, including Title IX. Job Description: The Curry Undergraduate Education Department is seeking submissions to a general pool for a variety of part time, associate lecturer teaching positions. Applicants who have current or recent experience in educational settings are preferred. The dept. is seeking candidates with a strong history of teaching PreK to 12 or higher education.  In your cover letter please indicate your ability to teach in a face to face format during the day (8:30-4:30) and/or evenings (4:00-7:30). Anticipated openings include The Teaching of Reading, Classroom Assessment and Data, Strategies for the Effective Educator, Fundamentals of Curriculum: Social Studies and Writing, MTEL Preparation/Intro to Writing, Introduction to Education Master's Degree in Education required. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Masters Degree in Education required. Salary : $3,735 per 3 credit course *Please note: Eligibility for promotion to Lecturer and an increased rate of compensation are negotiated between the College and the Curry College AAUP. Additional Information: Committed to attracting and retaining a diverse staff, Curry College will honor your experiences, perspectives and unique identity. Together, our community strives to create and maintain working and learning environments that are inclusive, equitable and welcoming. At the College's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be excepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the College, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Employment in this position is contingent upon the successful completion of all required pre-employment background checks. Title IX Notice of Nondiscrimination Curry College (the \"College\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits sex discrimination in any education program or activity that we administer, as required by Title IX and its federal regulations, including in admission and employment. The Non-Discrimination Policy can be found at https://www.curry.edu/assets/Documents/About-Us/Curry-College-Nondiscrimination-Policy.pdf The Sexual Misconduct Policy can be found at https://www.curry.edu/assets/Documents/About-Us/Curry-College-Sexual-Misconduct-Policy.pdf Individuals who wish to make a complaint of discrimination or sex discrimination under Title IX, or those with information about conduct that may constitute discrimination or sex discrimination under Title IX may contact the Director of Title IX and Equity Compliance, the Office for Civil Rights, or both. Inquiries about the implementation of Title IX and its federal regulations to the College may be referred to either or both offices listed below: Juan M. Hernandez, Ed.D, Vice President for Diversity, Equity, and Belonging, Interim Title IX and Section 504 Coordinator: Office 121, King Administrative Building, 55 Atherton Street Milton, MA. 02186. 617-333-2394, juan.hernandez@curry.edu Office of Civil Rights (\"OCR\") : Boston Office, Office for Civil Rights, US Department of Education, 9th Floor, 5 Post Office Square, Boston, MA 02109-3921, Telephone: 617-289-0111, FAX: 617-289-0150; TDD: 800-877-8339, Email: OCR.Boston@ed.gov. Application Instructions: Please apply online at https://www.curry.edu/about-us/community-resources/employment/job-opportunities for consideration. Interested applicants must submit the following: a curriculum vitae; cover letter; a statement of your teaching philosophy; a statement of contributions to diversity (statement addressing past and/or potential contributions to diversity through teaching, research, professional activity and/or service); a copy of your unofficial transcript (an official transcript will be required upon acceptance of an offer of employment); and a list of three professional references, one of which must be a former or current supervisor, including complete contact information and professional titles. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Curry College 1071 Blue Hill Ave, Milton, MA 02186"
    },
    "https://curry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=199585": {
      "title": "Part-Time Nursing Faculty",
      "description": "Curry College\nJob Posting: Part-Time Nursing Faculty Curry College \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Nursing Faculty Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Nursing Faculty Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Milton, MA Posted: Apr 16, 2026 Closes: Oct 31, 2028 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Part-time Position ID: 199585 Share About Curry College: Curry College, founded in 1879, is a private, four-year, liberal arts-based institution in Milton, Massachusetts. Curry is the only college in Massachusetts to guarantee students a job after graduation via The Curry Commitment program. The College is accredited by the New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE) and offers 28 undergraduate majors, over 50 minors and concentrations, seven graduate programs, and an associate's degree. The College boasts a wide array of co-curricular activities including 40+ student-run clubs and organizations and 19 NCAA Division III athletic teams. The Curry College mission is to educate and graduate students prepared to engage in successful careers and active citizenship with a global perspective. We are an inclusive community of diverse learners and educators, committed to continuing our legacy of developing effective communicators with reflective and critical thinking skills. We mentor and empower our students, building meaningful relationships that inspire them to achieve their ambitions. Curry College provides rigorous and relevant academic programs to undergraduate and graduate students, and our rich blend of liberal arts and career-directed programs is enhanced by practical field experiences and co-curricular activities. Learning at Curry extends beyond the classroom and is embedded in all that we do. Diversity and a culture of equity and inclusion among students, faculty and staff are crucial to the mission statement of Curry College. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, sex identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law, including Title IX. Job Description: Curry College has ongoing needs for part-time Faculty to teach in our Nursing Programs. We have a variety of track options at both the undergraduate and graduate level. Part-time Faculty are responsible for planning and presenting the material assigned for their courses and/or clinics/labs/simulations; defining specific requirements and communicating them to students; evaluating clinical performance, examinations and/or assignments, submitting grades promptly, and providing students with clear explanations of their evaluations. Part-time Faculty are expected to be available to interact electronically with students outside the classroom. Courses available may include didactic, clinical, lab, or simulation. The days and hours vary depending upon the course. There is often a need for faculty to instruct the clinical portion of our nursing courses. Requirements: For Classroom teaching, a minimum of a Master's Degree in Nursing (MSN) degree is required. Prior teaching experience preferred. For Clinical, Lab and Simulation based instruction, the requirements are 2 years of full-time nursing experience within the last 5 years and either an MSN degree or: hold a BSN and be matriculated in a graduate nursing program with an expected graduation date within five years of the date of the appointment; or possess a related non-nursing graduate degree; or possess a current nurse education certification by a board recognized certifying organization. In certain cases, candidates holding a BSN and possessing five years of full-time nursing experience within the past eight years may be considered but must be matriculated in a graduate nursing program within 1 year of appointment with an expected graduation date within 5 years of the date of matriculation or achieve nurse education certification by a board recognized certifying organization within 3 years of appointment) Curry College welcomes applications to teach in our Nursing Programs at any time. We continuously review application submissions for future needs. At this time there may not be an immediate vacancy in a particular area of clinical expertise, but candidates may provide their information to this posting for consideration for future opportunities. Salary: $1500 per credit (effective Fall 2026) *Please note: Eligibility for promotion to Lecturer and an increased rate of compensation are negotiated between the College and the Curry College AAUP. Additional Information: Committed to attracting and retaining a diverse staff, Curry College will honor your experiences, perspectives and unique identity. Together, our community strives to create and maintain working and learning environments that are inclusive, equitable and welcoming. At the College's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be excepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the College, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Employment in this position is contingent upon the successful completion of all required pre-employment background checks. Title IX Notice of Nondiscrimination Curry College (the \"College\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits sex discrimination in any education program or activity that we administer, as required by Title IX and its federal regulations, including in admission and employment. The Non-Discrimination Policy can be found at https://www.curry.edu/assets/Documents/About-Us/Curry-College-Nondiscrimination-Policy.pdf The Sexual Misconduct Policy can be found at https://www.curry.edu/assets/Documents/About-Us/Curry-College-Sexual-Misconduct-Policy.pdf Individuals who wish to make a complaint of discrimination or sex discrimination under Title IX, or those with information about conduct that may constitute discrimination or sex discrimination under Title IX may contact the Director of Title IX and Equity Compliance, the Office for Civil Rights, or both. Inquiries about the implementation of Title IX and its federal regulations to the College may be referred to either or both offices listed below: Juan M. Hernandez, Ed.D, Vice President for Diversity, Equity, and Belonging, Interim Title IX and Section 504 Coordinator: Office 121, King Administrative Building, 55 Atherton Street Milton, MA. 02186. 617-333-2394, juan.hernandez@curry.edu Office of Civil Rights (\"OCR\"): Boston Office, Office for Civil Rights, US Department of Education, 9th Floor, 5 Post Office Square, Boston, MA 02109-3921, Telephone: 617-289-0111, FAX: 617-289-0150; TDD: 800-877-8339, Email: OCR.Boston@ed.gov. Application Instructions: Please apply online at https://www.curry.edu/about-us/community-resources/employment/job-opportunities for consideration. Interested applicants must submit the following: a curriculum vitae; cover letter; a statement of your teaching philosophy; a statement of contributions to diversity (statement addressing past and/or potential contributions to diversity through teaching, research, professional activity and/or service); a copy of your unofficial transcript (an official transcript will be required upon acceptance of an offer of employment); and a list of three professional references, one of which must be a former or current supervisor, including complete contact information and professional titles. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Curry College 1071 Blue Hill Ave, Milton, MA 02186"
